# Local-dev API routes.
#
# `src/pages/api/**` holds LOCAL-ONLY API routes. Pages Router API routes are
# IGNORED by the production static export, so none of this reaches the deployed
# bundle — production serves /api natively from Cloudflare Pages Functions.
#
# Two kinds live here:
#   1. hand-written dev routes (invite, webhook-*, …) — tracked, authored by hand
#   2. GENERATED bridges produced by scripts/generate-pages-shims.mjs, which
#      invoke the real `functions/api/**` handler so `next dev` serves the same
#      API production does. These are committed rather than gitignored: the
#      generator's output location and filename convention have already changed
#      once, and a path-based ignore list silently let generated files through.
#      Regeneration is idempotent (`npm run generate:pages-shims --check`), so
#      they stay in sync and diffs stay clean.
#
# Do NOT add a build step that deletes them — that breaks any dev server that is
# already running.
services/**/.env
apps/**/.env

